ook different but  this new point of view could be even  more interesting you can also find out  more about restaurants hotels and rides  that you would like to try as a grownup  you will love to ride the rock and  roller coaster starring Aerosmith and  the twilight zone tower terror and then  eat roast lamb while watching belly  dancers at restaurant Marrakesh magic  still exists as long as you can believe  in it don't forget your Fastpass  the  best thing to do is to visit Disneyland  when there are not a lot of people there  but it is not always possible people  don't go on vacation during the summer  Christmas break and spring break because  they like to be surrounded by a lot of  people they do it because that's the  only time when they have the chance  sometimes there are so many people out  there that you are lucky to go on three  rides in one day during the worst days  you can wait at least an hour for a ride  and even up to two hours and there will  be a line again if you ever want to eat  or go to the bathroom this is why you  must get fast paths to make things a  little better the service is included in  the price of theme park admission and  you can get up to three selections for  each day but to go on the best rides at  the best time you'll have to plan up to  30 days in advance with a ticket and 60  prior to check-in if you stay at a hotel  however don't think that you can miss  your Fastpass window if you are too late  or too early you won't have the chance  to go on a ride a Fast Pass is a  privilege so make sure that you use it  the right way don't be rude to cast  members we understand that you spent two  hours waiting in line to go on Radiator  Springs racers or maybe you wanted to  meet Cinderella and she had to go on a  break before you could even go near her  and we were all upset when we realized  that we barely did anything that day  because there were too many people but  none of these things are a good reason  to be rude to cast members they are  doing their best and they don't like it  either when there are too many people  and they have probably met a lot of  angry customers before you so you don't  want to be the next one the cast member  will always keep a smile on their face  and will never break character no matter  what happens the best thing you can do  is make an effort to smile back some  people say that working at Disney World  and being around children and their  parents all day every day taught them  how not to raise their children some of  them even say that they often leave work  in tears and if you ever hear a cast  member tell someone to have a Disney day  it means that they have been dealing  with a difficult customer you don't want  to be that person cast members are doing  a lot of things for you so never forget  to be nice to them don't wear a costume  little girls wish they could become a  Disney Princess and the young boys hope  they will grow up to be just like their  favorite heroes Disneyland is the best  place to not only meet our favorite  characters but also be like them but  unfortunately that won't be happening if  you are an adult  that's because anyone over 14 years old  doesn't have the right to wear a costume  guests don't have the right to wear a  mask or even a cape if the length goes  below the waist if you ever go to the  theme park wearing some of these things  they have the right to deny admission or  ask you to remove the costume even when  dressing for special events grown-ups  don't have the right to pose for  pictures or sign autographs for other  guests and their costumes can't reach  the ground we understand these rules  after all we wouldn't want a prince not  so charming to earn the trust of a child  they don't know but it is still sad to  think that we will never get the chance  to become a true Disney Princess and  don't worry there are still some things  you can do accessories like transparent  wings plastic lightsabers and tutus are  acceptable and 